<title>USA: Intel posts Q3 shr $1.48 vs $1.05.</title>
<headline>Intel posts Q3 shr $1.48 vs $1.05.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>INTEL CORPORATION</p>
<p>			CONSOLIDATED SUMMARY FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p>
<p>			   (Millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p> INCOME			3 Months Ended	  9 Months Ended</p>
<p>				  Sep 28,   Sep 30,  Sep 28,  Sep 30,</p>
<p>				     1996	1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> NET REVENUE		  $ 5,142   $ 4,171  $14,407  $11,622</p>
<p> Cost of sales		  2,201     2,008    6,772    5,422</p>
<p> Research and development     449	 334    1,288	944</p>
<p>Marketing, general and</p>
<p>  administrative		  565	 440    1,600    1,274</p>
<p>Operating costs and</p>
<p>  expenses			3,215     2,782    9,660    7,640</p>
<p> OPERATING INCOME	     1,927     1,389    4,747    3,982</p>
<p> Interest and other		91	  94	248	316</p>
<p> INCOME BEFORE TAXES	  2,018     1,483    4,995    4,298</p>
<p> Income taxes		     706	 552    1,748    1,599</p>
<p> NET INCOME		     1,312	 931    3,247    2,699</p>
<p> EARNINGS PER SHARE	    1.48	1.05     3.67     3.06</p>
<p>COMMON SHARES AND</p>
<p>  EQUIVALENTS		     885	 889	884	883</p>
<p>NOTE: Intel latest Q3 earnings per share of $1.48 compares with $1.05 in the year-ago period. Analysts' consensus estimate for the latest Q3 was $1.25, according to First Call.</p>
</text>
